--[[
`nupp` holds the remaining storage and portable text-buffer APIs. Library code
uses the standard roots directly:

```nupp
local encoded = serde.json.encodevalue({ok = true})
debug.log.info("wrote %d bytes", #encoded)
```

Host requests use `os.host`, independent random generators use `math.random`,
and provider contracts use `package.nupp`. Storage and text buffers retain
`nupp.mem` and `nupp.text`. Private implementation modules remain beneath
`nupp`; application imports use the documented public module names.

See [standard-library.md](docs/learn/runtime/data/standard-library.md) for the
library overview and [modules.md](docs/learn/language/modules.md) for module
lookup.
]]

const nupp = {}
return nupp
